            %br/
          %h3#IngredientsOfFundamentalPhysics Ingredients of fundamental physics
          %p
            Ever since
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isaac+Newton"} Isaac Newton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories+of+physics"} theories of physics
            are formulated in the language of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            that we discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics#GEOMETRY"} geometry of physics - Geometry
          %p
            The physics that we are concerned with is
            %em fundamental
            physics, that part of the large subject of physics which is concerned with elementary processes and phenomena of physics from which all others are thought to
            %em emerge
            as approximations to collective effects of complex configurations of the elementary entities.
          %p
            The best
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            of fundamental physics as presently understood is known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac-Higgs+theory"} Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac-Higgs theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em free parameters
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            are such parameters, as is their coupling to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force+fields"} force fields
          %p
            Specifying these parameters is called constructing a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            in physics and specifically a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenological model
            of fundamental physics, if aimed at making the observations that are predicted by the theory to closely match those that are being made in experiments. The global choice of these parameters that make the predictions match all available data to the currently best possible degree is called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em standard model
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            for the sector in which the large-scale description of the force of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            is approximately negligible, and the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} standard model of cosmology
            which focuses on that large scale structure.
          %p The following table list some key ingredients of the standard theory of fundamental physics, all of which we discuss in detail further below.
