          %p
            In its traditional formulation, one considers the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            which is naturally induced by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian"} local Lagrangian
            on its (reduced)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            and says that a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+prequantization"} geometric prequantization
            of this form is the choice of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            on the phase space whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\nabla
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi prequantum
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi circle
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi bundle
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ∇
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi F
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mi curvature
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi PhaseSpace
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ω
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi sympl
                          %mo .
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi form
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\\
                  {{prequantum} \atop {circle\;bundle}} &amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F_{(-)}}} &amp; curvature
                  \\\
                  \&amp;PhaseSpace
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\omega}{\to}&amp;
                  \\Omega^2_{cl}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  sympl.\;form
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi ℂ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi Ψ
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi id
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; P \times_{U(1)}\mathbb{C}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\Psi}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{id}{\to}&amp; X
                  }
          %p
            is called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"} wave function
            on phase space. One is to choose a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            of phase space, equipping it locally with “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinates"}> canonical coordinates
            ” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momenta"}> canonical momenta
            ”. Then a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            in geometric quantization is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"} wave function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
            which only depends on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinates"} canonical coordinates
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi wave
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi functions
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi of
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi canonical
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi coordinates
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mi polarized
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi sections
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi of
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi prequantum
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi line
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi bundle
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z(\Sigma_{n-1})
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\{wave\; functions\;of\;canonical\;coordinates\}
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left\{
                  polarized\;sections\;of\;prequantum\;line\;bundle
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            From this it is clear that in order to refine this to local (extended, multi-tiered)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            we are to assign
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} higher line bundles
            in higher codimension, namely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantum (n-k)-bundle
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            As a first indication that this makes good sense, notice that the natural assignment to a field in codimension 0, hence to a field configuration on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+0-bundle"} prequantum 0-bundle
          %p So we are after a picture as indicated in the following table.
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                %th
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} local/extended Lagrangian field theory
                %th
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+quantum+field+theory"} local/extended quantum field theory
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  closed piece of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
