          %h3#IntermezzoElementsOfHigherCohesiveGeometry Intermezzo: Recalling elements of higher cohesive geometry
          %p
            The idea of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} extended prequantum field theory
            indicated
            %a{:href => "#TopologcalLocalLagrangianFieldTheoryInHigherGeometry"} above
            is best illustrated by the example of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+field+theory"} Chern-Simons field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CSAsArchetypicalExample"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesive
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            %em
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics#SmoothnGroupoids"} geometry of physics - smooth homotopy types
            and
            %em
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics#MaurerCartanForms"} geometry of physics - Maurer-Cartan forms
            and
            %em
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics#PrincipalConnections"} geometry of physics - principal connections
          %p
            Fix some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            of test spaces which encode some notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subsite"} dense subsite
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            on manifolds of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
            (which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
            does).
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaves"} (2,1)-sheaves
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"}> stacks
            ) on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi le
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh_{(2,1)}(\mathcal{C})
                  \\simeq
                  L_{le} Func(\mathcal{C}^{op}, Grpd)
                  \\,.
          %p
            of that of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            at the
            = succeed "." do
              %em local equivalences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(\mathcal{C})
            is the result of turning
            = succeed "-wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
            into actual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
          %p
            For the running example of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
            we may think of an object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(\mathcal{C})
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
          %p
            The higher refinement of groupoids which we need are
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            or (compactly generated weakly Hausdorff)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            universally turned into actual
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi whe
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi whe
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\infty Grpd \simeq L_{whe} sSet \simeq L_{whe} Top
          %p
            The combination of these two aspects, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            for the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"}> simplicial presheaves
            ) with the local (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"}> stalk
            \-wise)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            universally turned into actual homotopy equivalences:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo ≔
