                  \\stackrel{[\mathbf{\Pi}(S^1), \tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{p}_2]}{\to}
                  \&amp;
                  [\mathbf{\Pi}(S^1), \mathbf{B}^7 U(1)]
                  \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                  \\mathbf{B}^6 U(1) // \mathbf{B}^6 U(1)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the lower factorization of this map shows canonically that this 6-bundle is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant"} equivariant
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+action"} adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
            on itself, the analog of the ordinary adjoint equivariance of the ordinary WZW 2-bundle.
          %p
